    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by the high-upside combination of **Junior Caminero** (70.80) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (64.80). **Junior Caminero** remains an elite play today against Alcantara despite a neutral park adjustment, as he benefits significantly from a favorable SP_xERA of 4.46 and a dynamic platoon advantage. Meanwhile, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** earns his high score primarily through a massive 14% platoon boost; while his spot in the 8-hole and the opposing catcher\u2019s elite hold rate (60% SB) provide a slight drag on his ceiling, his speed-centric profile makes him an essential start given our priority on the scarcest category. **Casey Schmitt** also presents a strong value (63.92) as he capitalizes on a favorable matchup against Severino (4.63 xERA) and an elevated batting order position that offsets the minor penalty from the opposing catcher's pop time.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involves **Hyeseong Kim**, who landed just outside the active threshold with a 47.96 score. While **Hyeseong Kim** carries a solid floor due to platoon utility, his status at the bottom of the order (-8% adjustment) ultimately rendered him less efficient than options like **Chase Meidroth** or **Gary Sanchez**. We are keeping a close eye on **Yordan Alvarez**, who faces the stiffest test of the day against deGrom. While **Yordan Alvarez** maintains a respectable 54.65 score due to his elite xwOBA (0.425), the 19% penalty from the SP\u2019s skill set is a notable risk that could lead to a disappointing output if deGrom locates effectively. We also note that **Luke Raley** offers sneaky upside today; his score of 62.62 is buoyed by a 4% efficiency boost stemming from the opposing pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, which we project will provide a clear path for **Luke Raley** to execute on the basepaths.",
